[sub_resource type="StyleBoxEmpty" id="StyleBoxEmpty_focus"]

; The record stamp: a hard gold rule around a see-through middle, so it reads as
; something pressed onto the panel rather than another chip laid on it. Sized by
; the node's own offsets, not by its text, because the script measures the box to
; place it beside the total.
; What the crowns and the score sit on. Dark and see-through: the level is still
; there behind this panel, with the ball drifting off through it, and a solid
; card would shut that out -- but white type over a bright level needs something
; to sit on, and outlines alone were doing all of that work.
[sub_resource type="StyleBoxFlat" id="StyleBoxFlat_card"]
